Let, [latex] \begin{aligned}
\theta ^*&=\frac{T_s-T}{T_s-T_\infty }\\
y^*&=\frac{y}{L}\\
\frac{dy^*}{dy}&=\frac{1}{L}\\
\frac{d\theta ^*}{dy}&=-\frac{dT}{dy}
\end{aligned}
[/latex] [latex] T_s \text{ and } T_\infty [/latex] are constant At boundary [latex] \begin{aligned}
q_{\text{conduction}}&=q_{\text{convection}}\\
-K_f\left.\begin{matrix}
\frac{dT}{dy}
\end{matrix}\right|_{y=0}&=h(T_s-T_\infty )\\
-K_f\frac{d}{dy}\left [ \frac{T_s-T}{T_s-T_\infty }h \right ]&=h\\
\frac{d\theta ^*}{dy}&=\frac{h}{K_f}\\
\end{aligned}[/latex] Applying chain rule [latex]\begin{aligned}
\frac{d\theta ^*}{dy^*}\frac{dy^*}{dy}&=\frac{h}{K_f}\\
\frac{d\theta ^*}{dy^*}\frac{1}{L}=\frac{h}{K_f}\\
\frac{d\theta ^*}{dy^*}=\frac{hL}{K_f}=\text{Nusselt Number}\\
Nu&=\frac{d\theta ^*}{dy^*}
\end{aligned}
 [/latex] Nu represents non dimensional temperature gradient.

